cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Universal Right-Triangle Reflection Sequence (Unequal Legs)"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vico
    family-names: Bonfioli
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
    email: vicobonfioli@gmail.com
abstract: >
  For every right triangle in the plane with positive unequal rational
  legs, the BFS orbit-growth sequence of its three side-reflections
  agrees with one common sequence u_d (OEIS A396406) through depth 32,
  and this is sharp: the (1,2) triangle deviates at depth 33. The
  natural all-depths universality conjecture is refuted: for every
  rational, indeed every algebraic, shape an explicit nontrivial kernel
  element (a conjugated product of glide-reflection squares) forces a
  first deviation at depth n_T between max(33, c_T) and 24 c_T + 8. The
  common sequence is exactly the orbit growth of the generic right
  triangle (transcendental leg ratio), whose group is virtually the
  lamplighter Z wr Z; its translation lattice 2(t-1)Z[t] and the kernel
  of every algebraic specialization are computed exactly, and the word
  metric is given by a closed form, word length = l_R + 2c with l_R and
  c explicit site-local closed forms, proved for every element (Lean
  theorem metricAll); that the closed form l_R is also the minimum over
  relaxed realisations is verified, not proved. For rational legs the group
  W_T is a dense, non-finitely-presented solvable group of derived length 3
  whose index-4 rotation subgroup is Z[zeta_T^{+-1}] x| Z; its stable norm is round,
  and its growth series is excluded from explicit low-complexity rational,
  algebraic and P-recursive boxes (non-D-finiteness is conjectural). In n
  dimensions the right-angled
  Coxeter envelope of the orthoscheme has rational growth with rate
  r_n = 1 + 2 cos(2 pi / (n+3)); for n >= 3 every kernel element of word
  length 6 lies in a rank-two standard parabolic, and the rank-two
  relations are classified by rank-0 descent on the elliptic curves
  24a1, 72a2 and y^2 = x^3 - x. These give the collision depth
  unconditionally on two of the three strata. On the third, the depth is
  infinite exactly when the affine representation is injective. The
  envelope W_n itself embeds in O(n), hence in Isom(R^n), for every
  n >= 3 (thm:alln), and n = 2 is the proved exception; injectivity of
  the affine representation at a given shape is a separate question, and
  its arithmetic Class C form is false, while the generic form holds for
  every n >= 3: the affine representation is injective for leg tuples with
  algebraically independent ratios, so the generic n-orthoscheme group is
  W_n, with rational growth series. The plane is therefore the only
  dimension in which the generic growth series is not rational. An earlier claim of
  unconditional faithfulness from det Q_n = -prod a_i^2 was a non
  sequitur and is withdrawn. On the
  arithmetic of the growth series, the Polya-Carlson dichotomy for the
  four catalytic blocks is unconditional, and the rational branch is
  excluded unconditionally for the two denominators, leaving the two
  numerators under an unproved coefficient-growth hypothesis. The travel
  resolvent is transcendental over Q(x) unconditionally. The growth
  series U = A396406 of the universal group and its relaxed companion V
  are transcendental over Q(x), with no hypotheses: the transfer model
  (M), the invariance of the travel block (T) and the junction pairing
  (R-J) are now theorems. Moreover U and V are not D-finite (u_n and v_n
  are not P-recursive) and |x| = 1 is a natural boundary of both; for the
  travel resolvent both statements are unconditional. The travel pole
  equation is a Fredholm determinant equal to the Hahn-Exton q-cosine, so
  the travel poles are its zeros. The transcendence proof is computer-assisted in two finite
  ranges (MPFR interval certificates at the first twelve travel poles
  and at the six gate poles above tau = 5e-3), and the assembly step of
  (M) is a hand proof that is not formalised. The growth rate is beta_2 = 1.4916177871..., which excludes
  3/2.
